        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8e1ce9df-0463-5535-9cbb-f491ae78877a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Reynolds Channel, Nassau County, New York, Long Island, Barnum Island, Lawrence, Atlantic Beach, Rockaway Peninsula\n- Structures: Atlantic Beach Bridge\n- Roads: NY 878, Park Street, Seagirt Boulevard\n- People: William Reynolds\n\nFacts:\n- Reynolds Channel is a strait in Nassau County, New York, named after William Reynolds.\n- Reynolds Channel separates the Long Beach Barrier Island from Long Island and Barnum Island.\n- The Long Beach Barrier Island contains the City of Long Beach and the villages of Atlantic Beach and Lido Beach.\n- The Atlantic Beach Bridge is a 153-foot-long toll drawbridge carrying NY 878.\n- The Atlantic Beach Bridge connects Lawrence and Atlantic Beach at Park Street, New York, by crossing the west end of Reynolds Channel.\n- The Atlantic Beach Bridge also provides direct access to the Rockaway Peninsula via Seagirt Boulevard.",
